Description: Local-first AI assistant with cross-device sessions and IM channel routing
 Hope Agent is a local-first AI assistant desktop app. Sessions hand off seamlessly across your devices and chats; memory accumulates over time and recurring work crystallizes into reusable skills. The single binary runs in three modes: desktop GUI, HTTP/WS daemon for headless deployment, and ACP stdio for IDE integrations. Built-in templates for mainstream LLM providers (Anthropic, OpenAI, Codex, plus local LLM via Ollama) cover the typical setup with a paste-the-API-key flow; IM channel integration covers Slack, Discord, Telegram, Feishu, WhatsApp, LINE, and more.

